---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/switch/from-simplepractice/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="growth-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/tools/">Resources</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">A plan for your SimplePractice records.</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="growth-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Switching from SimplePractice</div>
        <h1>A plan for your SimplePractice records.</h1>
        <p>
          We start with the exports you can obtain, then confirm how the
          receiving system will handle them.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="growth-answer">
        <strong>Before you begin</strong>
        <p>
          These are preparation steps for evaluating a move to Otto. Otto’s
          accepted imports, migration service, timing, and fees still need
          confirmation. There is no migration upload on this site.
        </p>
      </div>
      <section class="growth-section prose">
        <h2>1. Confirm access and responsibility.</h2>
        <p>
          Identify who may export the practice’s records, which clients are in
          scope, who will retain the original records, and how the export will
          be stored and transferred securely.
        </p>
        <h2>2. Understand the source export.</h2>
        <p>
          SimplePractice documents exports under{" "}
          <strong>Settings → Practice → Data export</strong>. The account owner
          or a practice manager with data-export permissions chooses a scope and
          export type. Its guide distinguishes Complete, Sessions, and Contacts
          exports.
        </p>
        <p>
          Keep password protection enabled and retrieve files while the export
          is available. Review restricted-client settings and the resulting
          contents. The guide says appointment data needs a separate report; the
          Contacts export uses vCard rather than a spreadsheet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Use the{" "}
          <a href="https://support.simplepractice.com/hc/en-us/articles/207625506-Exporting-client-information-through-data-exports">
            current SimplePractice export guide
          </a>{" "}
          for the exact steps and contents. A Complete export does not establish
          that Otto can import every included item.
        </p>
        <h2>3. Match each record category to a destination.</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Record category</th>
                <th>Acceptance question for Otto</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Demographics and insurance</td>
                <td>Which fields and file formats are supported?</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Historical notes and signatures</td>
                <td>
                  Can we preserve dates, authorship, signature information, and
                  readability?
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Attachments and forms</td>
                <td>
                  What uploads are supported, and how will they attach to the
                  correct client?
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Appointments and balances</td>
                <td>Can these transfer, or will the practice recreate them?</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Audit and access records</td>
                <td>
                  What stays in an accessible archive, and who owns retention?
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <h2>4. Test, reconcile, and plan cutover.</h2>
        <p>
          Use an agreed sample to compare counts, dates, labels, and document
          contents. Keep an exception list and resolve mismatches before
          approving a broader move. Budget overlap time using the{" "}
          <a href="/tools/ehr-cost-calculator/">EHR cost calculator</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="growth-section migration-checklist">
        <span class="eyebrow">Your preparation checklist</span>
        <h2>Keep track of the next steps.</h2>
        <p>
          Check items as you review them. This checklist stays in the current
          page; download a copy to keep your progress.
        </p>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Export permission and
          record ownership confirmed
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Record categories and
          counts inventoried
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Otto import scope,
          costs, and timeline confirmed
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Secure transfer method
          agreed
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Sample transferred and
          checked
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Exceptions resolved and
          retention plan approved
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-migration-item /> Cutover and client
          communications planned
        </label>
        <button
          class="button"
          id="migration-download"
          data-vendor="SimplePractice"
        >
          Download checklist
        </button>
      </section>
      <div class="tool-support">
        <a href="/compare/otto-vs-simplepractice/">
          Compare Otto and SimplePractice ↗
        </a>
        <a href="/security/">Review data questions ↗</a>
        <a href="/waitlist/">Discuss your practice ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sources">
        <h2>Sources and review</h2>
        <p>
          Sources checked October 16, 2026. Confirm current product terms before
          choosing software.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://support.simplepractice.com/hc/en-us/articles/207625506-Exporting-client-information-through-data-exports">
              SimplePractice export documentation
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <script is:inline src="/assets/documents.js"></script>
      <script is:inline src="/assets/migration.js" defer></script>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
